Down in the mimic version of minds end (well, there's a freudian slip, I
think I'll keep it), my monk had been sensing a mind flayer wandering
around, so I was engraving E frequently when I didn't see any #s
nearby. Then just out of range came the 3 I knew must be it, while I was
trapped in one of the little rooms. A quick E-word and only five taps of
the space bar later, and there was the little brainsucker himself, turning
to flee.

Now, Hito had only the protection spell, but a quiverful of poisoned
darts, so I figured I knew just how to take care of old purple and
wrinkly. But I knew how easily engravings could be marred by lots of
movement, so I figured I needed more protection. I made sure everything
was spelled properly the first time, then decided to add two more
iterations. Oops; YASD came swiftly.

This surprised me. I thought that as long as I was standing on a complete
Elbereth, I would be protected while adding more. Obviously, I was
mistaken, but why?



